{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_926498109#7_1925541721","relevance":3,"reason":"The passage directly answers the need: after Bell's telephone debuted in 1876, initial excitement waned, customers were scarce, Bell Telephone seemed unlikely to survive, and Western Union's William Orton dismissed it as an 'electrical toy.'","learned":"Early reactions were mixed: the telephone initially drew attention as a technological wonder, but public/customer interest faded and a major telegraph executive dismissed it as a toy."},"action":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"initial excitement waned\" \"customers were scarce\" telephone)","reason":"Search the distinctive direct wording from this strong result to find additional sources documenting that early enthusiasm for the telephone faded and customers were scarce."}}
{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ \"initial excitement waned\" \"customers were scarce\" telephone)"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_24_926498109#6_1925540477","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1762","rank":1,"snippet":"Service What AT&T Did (and Still Does) Transmission Switching Management The End of Monopoly After the Breakup SBC: Ma Bell's Heir Apparent? \" , \"segment\": \"Bell spilled liquid on his desk and said reflexively, \\\"Watson come here, I need you.\\\" Watson wasn't within earshot, but he heard the request just the same. He received the call from the telephone. A patent attorney, Hubbard had already filed patents in Bell's name for the device. Now he and Sanders formed a company to sell this new invention to the world: the Bell telephone. At first the telephone got quite a bit of attention as a technological wonder, debuting at the Philadelphia Centennial Exhibition on July 25, 1876. But the <cover>initial excitement waned and customers were scarce. Bell returned to Scotland and left the business operations to Hubbard. Without visionary leadership, Bell Telephone </cover>looked as if it wouldn't last the decade, much less conquer the next century.\" , \"start_char\": 2891.000000 , \"title\": \"How AT&T Works | HowStuffWorks\" , \"url\": \"https://money.howstuffworks.com/att.htm\" }"}}
