{"request":{"op":"query","query":"(^ (+ telephone telephones) (+ \"early adoption\" \"early users\" \"social history\" \"nineteenth century\") (+ resistance resisted suspicion anxiety fear privacy))"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_11_491165450#4_858136133","ok":true,"op":"query","qid":"q1768","rank":1,"snippet":"3811.000000 , \"headings\": \"DIME DIME Feedback Flashcards & Bookmarks ? References in periodicals archive ? Acronyms browser ? Full browser ? \" , \"segment\": \"Dime launches two unique products The government's free Wi-Fi Internet access, and the Bureau of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources' national fisheries program are also be subject to Project DIME. DBM to use drones, satellites to monitor projects Contemporary concerns about the potential dangers of social networking sites and mobile communication devices, evidenced by the increasing incidence of cyberbullying, \\\"sexting,\\\" and <cover>privacy violations are not all that different from nineteenth century concerns about dime novels, the telegraph, telephone, </cover>photography, and the phonograph, not to mention twentieth century media like film, radio, and comic books. \"Pernicious stuff\": nineteenth century media, the children who loved them, and the adults who worried about them The Dimes ' last release, \"The Silent Generation,\" also had a historical theme, but Clay said that's not all the band plans to do. Boppin' In Beantown Confident the Dime will not have the typical short-lived span for an L.A. Once upon a Dime: the Dime has survived its first year as a no-frills, paparazzi-free "}}
