{"latest_judgment":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_1339911292#13_2782357850","relevance":2,"reason":"The passage includes a direct Western Union 1876 quote saying the telephone had too many shortcomings and no value, which supports early skepticism. However, the document is about project management/leadership rather than the telephone, so the evidence is incidental rather than dedicated.","learned":"The Western Union rejection quote is repeated in non-telephone contexts as an example of failed innovation judgment."},"action":{"op":"next","qid":"q1769","reason":"The query is retrieving the strong Western Union rejection quote; continue to find more telephone-focused documents with direct evidence of early distrust or skepticism."}}
{"request":{"op":"next","qid":"q1769"},"response":{"docno":"msmarco_v2.1_doc_49_1339911292#12_2782355991","ok":true,"op":"next","qid":"q1769","rank":3,"snippet":"Quality Mangement Stress Management Lesson Learned In Conclusion \" , \"segment\": \"Change Management; Quality Management; Stress management. Leadership Path In the presentation, “Mission Possible: Effectively Managing a Crashed and Fastracked Shorten Interval Project” examples are given of project experiences that co-relate to each of the subcategories below on the Leadership Path and the Project Management Path. For the purposes of this paper, a brief highlight of the topic will be given with further elaboration to be given with examples a the conference presentation. Vision Behind every good project, a great leader should be found. Lack of leadership vision can have detrimental effects on a project and opportunities could be lost. Consider this statement from the <cover>Western Union Internal Memo 1876, “ The ‘telephone’ has too many shortcomings </cover>to be seriously considered as a means of communication. The device is inherently of no value to us” (Western Union Internal memo 1876, 2005).\" , \"start_char\": 6937.000000 , \"title\": \"Managing Crashed & Fastracked Shorten Interval Project\" , \"url\": \"https://www.pmi.org/learning/library/managing-crashed-fastracked-shorten-interval-project-7603\" }"}}
